# Reviewer defaults (when + how light)

**Default bias: skip or go light.** Do not launch `code-reviewer` (or any reviewer) on every change. Prefer implement + targeted verify. See [lean-loop](lean-loop.mdc).

## When to skip reviewers entirely

| Situation | Reviewers |
|-|-|
| **Direct** (feedback / finetune / bugfix) | **None** - parent verifies; skip unless auth/secrets risk or human asks |
| **micro-S** Feature (copy, config, tiny obvious fix) | **None** - generator/parent gates enough |
| **Docs-only / changelog-only** | **None** (doc-updater only if user-facing docs need sync) |
| Rubric says `reviewers: none` or deferred | Honor that |

## When to run (Feature track)

Launch **only** the specialists the change actually needs. Prefer **specialists over a heavy general code review**.

| Change type | Default subagents | Skip |
|-|-|--|
| **S** (small, non-auth, non-API) | **None** or optional light `code-reviewer` if risk is unclear | Don’t add others |
| **M+ general code** | Light `code-reviewer` | Don’t add specialists you don’t need |
| **UI only** | `frontend-evaluator` only if design HTML / wireframe exists or L/XL; light `code-reviewer` **only if** non-trivial logic | api/mcp/db; skip frontend-eval for S-M with no design artefacts |
| **API / routes** (no new auth) | `api-reviewer` | security unless trust boundary changed; skip heavy code-reviewer if api-reviewer covers it |
| **MCP** | `mcp-reviewer` + `security-reviewer` | - |
| **DB / migrations / RLS** | `database-reviewer` + `security-reviewer` | RLS only if introduced; Dockyard control plane uses SQLite/goose |
| **Auth / secrets / trust** | `security-reviewer` (+ light `code-reviewer` if large) | api unless new public contract |
| **Perf / budgets** | `performance-evaluator` | - |

**Rule of thumb:** one specialist > stacking `code-reviewer` + specialist for the same concern. Do not launch the full roster.

## How light is code-reviewer

When `code-reviewer` **does** run:

- Diff-only, ≤~25 lines feedback, CRITICAL/HIGH only (≤3 optional notes)
- Trust generator’s already-run gates - re-run only if missing or suspicious
- No style essays, no whole-repo audit, no MEDIUM/LOW catalogs
- Prefer faster model

## Always

- **`doc-updater`** last only if required reviewers ran and PASS (or no reviewers required and docs need update).
- Parent consolidates BLOCK → auto-continue generator (≤3) - do not ask human to approve reviews.
- Prefer smaller set; when unsure, **skip** code-reviewer rather than launch “just in case.”

## Stop early (do not auto-loop)

After iteration **1**, pause and re-clarify when:

- `security-reviewer` returns **CRITICAL**, or
- `frontend-evaluator` **FAIL** (wrong wireframe / product intent)

All other BLOCKs → auto generator i+1 without asking.
